quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  5,96,"You are permitted to hunt and eat seafood as a provision for you and the travellers. But you have been forbidden the game of the land so long as you remain in pilgrim sanctity. And be God-conscious, to Whom you shall be gathered."
  5,97,"Allah has made the Ka‘ba, the Sacred House, a sanctuary of well-being for people, and (also) the sacred month, the offering (of the sacrificial animals) and garlands. All that (is ordained) so you may know that Allah knows whatever is in the heavens and whatever is on the earth, and that Allah is All-Knowing of everything."
  5,98,"Know that Allah is Severe in retribution, and Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
  5,99,"The Messenger’s responsibility is only to communicate, and Allah knows what you reveal and what you conceal."
  5,100,"Say: ‘The good and the evil are not equal, though the abundance of evil may impress you. Be conscious of Allah, O possessors of intellect, that you may succeed.’"
  5,101,"O believers! Do not ask regarding things (the Qur’an is silent about) which, if they are made clear to you, may trouble you. And if you ask about them while the Qur’an is being revealed, they shall be disclosed to you (and you will be left with no discretion). Allah has (so far) excused these matters. And Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Forbearing."
  5,102,"Indeed, some people before you asked such questions, then became disbelievers on account of them."
  5,103,"Allah has not prescribed any such thing as Bahira, Sa’iba, Wasila and Ham.* But the disbelievers fabricate lies against Allah, and most of them do not understand."
